Implement a Verilog module that takes a 50 MHz clock signal, a reset input, and an output signal. The module should generate a reset pulse of 10 clock cycles duration when the reset input is asserted. The output signal should be high during the reset pulse and low otherwise. The reset pulse should occur only once per reset event.

Use the following module header:
```
module RESET(CLK, RST_I, RST_OUT);
    input CLK, RST_I;
    output RST_OUT;

    // Your code here

endmodule
```

code:
module RESET(CLK, RST_I, RST_OUT);
    input CLK, RST_I;
    output RST_OUT;

    reg [4:0] cnt;
    reg rst_pulse;

    always @(posedge CLK or negedge RST_I) begin
        if (!RST_I) begin
            cnt <= 0;
            rst_pulse <= 0;
        end
        else if (cnt == 10) begin
            rst_pulse <= 0;
        end
        else if (rst_pulse == 0) begin
            cnt <= cnt + 1;
            rst_pulse <= 1;
        end
    end

    assign RST_OUT = rst_pulse;

endmodule

